SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Staatsfinanzen stabilisieren, Zukunftsinvestitionen ausbauen, fiskalische Resilienz stärken","publisher":"Bundesministerium der Finanzen","publication_date":"2022-07-01","url":"https://www.bundesfinanzministerium.de/Content/DE/Pressemitteilungen/Finanzpolitik/2022/03/2022-03-16-bundeshaushalte-2022-2023.html","claim":"The cabinet adopted the 2022 supplementary budget and the 2023 budget framework, said fiscal policy was shifting back to stability, promised respect for the debt brake, and expanded future investment in climate, mobility, digitalization, innovation, education, research, and infrastructure.","locator":"lines 258-262","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct ministry budget press release with a dated cabinet decision and explicit fiscal priorities.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exactly within 2022 and directly relevant to Scholz's fiscal stewardship.","ruler_attribution":"Cabinet-level policy under Scholz; attributable to his government, though implementation depended on parliament and ministries.","contrary_evidence":["It was a draft budget, not final spending, and it still relied on extraordinary crisis-era financing assumptions."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.6","5B.7","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bundesregierung bringt zweites Entlastungspaket auf den Weg","publisher":"Bundesministerium der Finanzen","publication_date":"2022-04-27","url":"https://www.bundesfinanzministerium.de/Content/DE/Pressemitteilungen/Finanzpolitik/2022/04/2022-04-27-zweites-entlastungspaket.html","claim":"The cabinet agreed on a second relief package with a 300 euro energy allowance for taxable workers, a 100 euro child bonus, a temporary fuel-tax cut, and other measures intended to provide quick, unbureaucratic relief to households and families hit by higher energy prices.","locator":"lines 255-270","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official cabinet press release with precise policy instruments and amounts.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exactly within 2022 and directly on the ruler-period timeline.","ruler_attribution":"A Scholz-government package, though it was negotiated collectively with coalition partners and implemented through legislation.","contrary_evidence":["The package was temporary and addressed the shock rather than structural productivity or competitiveness problems."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.8","5B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"12 Euro Mindestlohn ab Oktober","publisher":"Deutscher Bundestag","publication_date":"2022-05-18","url":"https://www.bundestag.de/presse/hib/kurzmeldungen-896002","claim":"The Bundestag committee approved the government's bill to raise the statutory minimum wage to 12 euro per hour from 1 October 2022 and to raise the mini-job threshold to 520 euro, with rules meant to prevent misuse of mini-jobs as substitutes for regular employment.","locator":"lines 736-740","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official parliamentary reporting on a government bill and its concrete labor-market terms.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exactly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Government initiative within the Scholz coalition, though enacted through parliament and supported by coalition discipline.","contrary_evidence":["Critics in the committee said the change was an intervention in wage-setting and would not by itself solve low pay or poverty."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bundeskanzler Scholz: Wir müssen uns unterhaken","publisher":"Deutscher Bundestag","publication_date":"2022-07-06","url":"https://www.bundestag.de/dokumente/textarchiv/2022/kw27-de-regierungsbefragung-900498","claim":"Scholz said he had launched a Concerted Action involving unions, employers, the state, the Bundesbank, and the Council of Economic Experts, and he acknowledged that the government's earlier relief packages totaling 30 billion euro were not enough.","locator":"lines 736-738 and 747","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct Bundestag transcript of Scholz explaining his own coordination forum and follow-up process.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exactly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Scholz initiative, though the forum relied on other institutions and social partners for analysis and follow-up.","contrary_evidence":["This is coordination and agenda-setting, not proof that the next policy round was already optimal or complete."],"lenses":["5B.7","5B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Schutzschild der Bundesregierung für vom Krieg betroffene Unternehmen","publisher":"Bundesministerium für Wirtschaft und Klimaschutz","publication_date":"2022-04-08","url":"https://www.bmwk.de/Redaktion/DE/Pressemitteilungen/2022/04/20220408-bundesregierung-beschliesst-schutzschild.html","claim":"The federal government announced a shield for war-affected companies, including temporary gas and electricity cost damping, KfW-backed credit lines of up to 100 billion euro, and possible equity or hybrid-capital support for especially relevant firms.","locator":"bullet list in the press release summary","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official ministry release with concrete financing figures and policy design.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exactly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Government-level economic crisis response under Scholz, with implementation shared across coalition ministries and agencies.","contrary_evidence":["Emergency support of this sort can distort competition and increase fiscal risk."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.4","5B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Regierungserklärung von Bundeskanzler Olaf Scholz","publisher":"Die Bundesregierung","publication_date":"2022-10-20","url":"https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-de/service/newsletter-und-abos/bulletin/regierungserklaerung-von-bundeskanzler-olaf-scholz-2137018","claim":"Scholz announced a 200 billion euro economic defense shield to cap gas and heating prices, said the design came from a commission including scientists, employers, unions, municipal utilities, and energy suppliers, and said the plan would make energy affordable while preserving savings incentives.","locator":"lines 247-251","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct Scholz speech with explicit policy announcement, rationale, and scope.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exactly within 2022 and squarely within the crisis year.","ruler_attribution":"Direct personal announcement by Scholz, though the policy was prepared collectively and still required implementation.","contrary_evidence":["A price shield of this scale is expensive and can be less targeted than narrower transfers."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.7","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Sicherung der Gasversorgung: Bundesregierung überführt Gasunternehmen SEFE ins Eigentum des Bundes – Kapitalmaßnahmen angeordnet","publisher":"Bundesministerium für Wirtschaft und Klimaschutz","publication_date":"2022-11-14","url":"https://www.bmwk.de/Redaktion/DE/Pressemitteilungen/2022/11/20221114-sicherung-der-gasversorgung-bundesregierung-uberfuhrt-gasunternehmen-sefe-ins-eigentum-des-bundes.html","claim":"The government transferred SEFE into federal ownership and ordered capital measures to secure gas supply and avert insolvency that could have endangered Germany's energy security.","locator":"opening paragraph","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official ministry action notice with a direct ownership change and stated purpose.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exactly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"A Scholz-government intervention in the energy economy, though executed through the economics ministry and statutory emergency powers.","contrary_evidence":["This was an extraordinary rescue operation with clear fiscal and market-intervention costs."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bundeskabinett verabschiedet Gas- und Strompreisbremse – Wichtige Entlastung für Verbraucherinnen und Verbraucher und die Wirtschaft","publisher":"Bundesministerium für Wirtschaft und Klimaschutz","publication_date":"2022-11-25","url":"https://www.bmwk.de/Redaktion/DE/Pressemitteilungen/2022/20221125-bundeskabinett-verabschiedet-gas-und-strompreisbremse-wichtige-entlastung-fur-verbraucherinnen-und-verbraucher-und-die-wirtschaft.html","claim":"The cabinet approved gas, electricity, and heat price brakes as the core of the 200 billion euro defense shield, with caps for households and firms and application from March 2023 with January-February retroactive relief.","locator":"press release introduction and policy description","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official cabinet decision notice with detailed policy parameters and timing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exactly within 2022, though the measures took effect mainly in 2023.","ruler_attribution":"Cabinet-level decision under Scholz, with joint drafting by the Chancellery, Finance Ministry, and Economics Ministry.","contrary_evidence":["The price brakes were temporary and highly costly, so they are relief rather than structural reform."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.3","5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Leistungen der Entlastungspakete","publisher":"Bundesministerium der Finanzen","publication_date":"2022-07","url":"https://www.bundesfinanzministerium.de/Monatsberichte/2022/07/Inhalte/Kapitel-2b-Schlaglicht/Tabelle/interview-entlastungspakete.html","claim":"The ministry's table summarized the relief packages as including EEG-levy abolition, fuel-tax cuts, a 350 euro heating subsidy for some housing-benefit recipients, the 300 euro energy allowance, the 100 euro child bonus, a 200 euro payment for some social-benefit recipients, a 100 euro payment for some unemployment-benefit recipients, and the 9 euro public-transport ticket.","locator":"table rows 134-140","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official ministry summary table with explicit benefit amounts and recipient groups.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Targets 2022 relief policy directly.","ruler_attribution":"Coalition-level crisis relief under Scholz; the table is descriptive rather than a personal statement.","contrary_evidence":["These were temporary shock absorbers rather than long-run productivity reforms."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.8","5B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bürgergeld-Gesetz (Regelbedarfsstufen)","publisher":"Deutscher Bundestag","publication_date":"2022-11-10","url":"https://www.bundestag.de/parlament/plenum/abstimmung/abstimmung?id=809","claim":"The Bundestag passed the government's Bürgergeld bill in November 2022; the debate centered on higher standard rates, qualification, bureaucracy reduction, and whether the reform truly overcame poverty and Hartz IV.","locator":"lines 823-825","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official parliamentary vote record and debate summary for a government bill.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exactly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Scholz-government legislation, though enacted through parliamentary coalition bargaining.","contrary_evidence":["Opponents argued the reform still left people in poverty and did not fully replace Hartz IV's coercive logic."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Entwicklung des Arbeitsmarkts 2022 in Deutschland","publisher":"Bundesagentur für Arbeit","publication_date":"2022-11-30","url":"https://www.arbeitsagentur.de/news/arbeitsmarkt-vorjahre","claim":"By late November 2022 the labor market was described as stable, with employment still growing even as unemployment, underemployment, and short-time work rose because of the strained economic environment.","locator":"November 2022 section, lines 479-483","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official labor-agency reporting with contemporaneous monthly labor-market data.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exactly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Context and outcome evidence rather than a direct Scholz policy act, but relevant to his government's crisis management.","contrary_evidence":["The same report notes rising unemployment and short-time work, showing genuine stress beneath the stable headline."],"lenses":["5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"OECD Economic Surveys: Germany 2023","publisher":"OECD","publication_date":"2023","url":"https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/oecd-economic-surveys-germany-2023_9642a3f5-en.html","claim":"The OECD said Russia's war disrupted Germany's recovery, energy-price spikes fuelled inflation and reduced household purchasing power, and the government acted swiftly to secure energy supply and support households and firms, while noting the relief measures could be better targeted.","locator":"Executive summary, lines 3761-3766","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent country survey with clear economic assessment and policy evaluation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"The report evaluates 2022 developments directly and provides a useful retrospective assessment.","ruler_attribution":"Primarily an assessment of Scholz's government response, not a personal act by Scholz alone.","contrary_evidence":["The OECD explicitly says the relief measures could have been better targeted and that the crisis hurt investment and purchasing power."],"lenses":["5B.7","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Germany: 2023 Article IV Consultation-Press Release; Staff Report; and Statement for Germany","publisher":"International Monetary Fund","publication_date":"2023-07-17","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/publications/cr/issues/2023/07/14/germany-2023-article-iv-consultation-press-release-staff-report-and-statement-by-the-536350","claim":"The IMF said Germany's economy showed resilience after the 2022 Russian gas shut-off, that the energy shock and tight financial conditions weighed on growth, and that the authorities' policy response to spillovers from Russia's war in Ukraine was timely and generally well designed.","locator":"summary and staff appraisal lines 265-267 and 268","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent IMF consultation report with explicit evaluation of policy response and macro effects.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly reviews the 2022 shock and the government's response.","ruler_attribution":"Assessment of the Scholz government's fiscal and crisis-management response, not personal authorship alone.","contrary_evidence":["The IMF also says growth was expected to stay slightly negative in 2023 and that uncertainty remained unusually high."],"lenses":["5B.7","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bruttoinlandsprodukt im Jahr 2022 um 1,9 % gestiegen","publisher":"Statistisches Bundesamt","publication_date":"2023-01-13","url":"https://www.destatis.de/DE/Presse/Pressemitteilungen/2023/01/PD23_020_811.html","claim":"Destatis reported that real GDP increased by 1.9 percent in 2022, while noting that the economy was shaped by the war in Ukraine, extreme energy-price increases, material shortages, delivery bottlenecks, and still-elevated pandemic effects.","locator":"lines 131-133","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official national statistics press release with exact 2022 macro outcome and stated drivers.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exactly covers the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Macroeconomic context and outcome, not direct proof of Scholz's personal competence, but relevant to the end-of-year trajectory.","contrary_evidence":["The growth rate was modest and heavily shock-driven, so it does not by itself prove strong ruler performance."],"lenses":["5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Inflationsrate im Jahr 2022 bei +7,9 %","publisher":"Statistisches Bundesamt","publication_date":"2023-01-17","url":"https://www.destatis.de/DE/Presse/Pressemitteilungen/2023/01/PD23_022_611.html","claim":"Destatis reported annual CPI inflation of 7.9 percent in 2022, with the surge driven primarily by extreme increases in energy and food prices after the start of the war in Ukraine.","locator":"lines 133-147","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official statistics release with precise annual inflation and stated driver analysis.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exactly covers the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Outcome context rather than a direct ruler act, but crucial for judging the government's crisis response.","contrary_evidence":["High inflation is a negative macro outcome and not something Scholz fully controlled."],"lenses":["5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Abrechnung der grundgesetzlichen Regel zur Begrenzung der Neuverschuldung (Schuldenbremse) 2022","publisher":"Bundesministerium der Finanzen","publication_date":"2023-09","url":"https://www.bundesfinanzministerium.de/Monatsberichte/2023/09/Inhalte/Kapitel-3-Analysen/3-1-abrechnung-schuldenbremse-2022.html","claim":"The 2022 federal structural net borrowing reached 8.09 percent of GDP, exceeding the debt-brake ceiling by 276.4 billion euro, including 179.4 billion euro for the Energy Stabilization Fund.","locator":"lines 139-143 and 155-159","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official retrospective fiscal accounting with explicit 2022 figures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective accounting for the target year 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Government-level fiscal record under Scholz, though partly driven by emergency authority and Bundestag declarations of exceptional conditions.","contrary_evidence":["The same report notes the exceptional situation tied to the pandemic and the Russian invasion of Ukraine, which complicates a simple blame reading."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Closed Cabinet meeting at Schloss Meseberg","publisher":"Federal Government","publication_date":"2022-08-30","url":"https://www.bundesregierung.de/breg-en/service/archive/kabinettklausur-meseberg-2082168","claim":"At Meseberg the cabinet discussed securing energy supply, the national security strategy, and digital strategy, with Scholz emphasizing that the government had to ensure citizens and businesses could handle the economic and financial consequences; Habeck and Lindner took part in the joint press conference and external experts and business/agency leaders were invited to the meeting.","locator":"lines 140-167, 187-197, and 223-227","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government archive page documenting cabinet deliberation and participation by the relevant economic ministers and outside experts.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exactly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Scholz-led cabinet process, though not a single-person economic appointment decision.","contrary_evidence":["The source is process evidence, not an audit of policy quality or outcomes."],"lenses":["5B.2","5B.7","5B.9"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I considered roughly 30 documents across the chancellery, BMF, BMWK, Bundestag, Bundesagentur für Arbeit, Destatis, OECD, IMF, and a few duplicate or derivative reporting pages. I retained the sources above because they each add a distinct policy, implementation, or outcome claim for 2022 and do not merely paraphrase the same package in another outlet.

I rejected or did not keep pages that were out of period, current-cabinet pages, generic background explainers, or duplicate ministry copies of the same relief measure. Several 2023 and later pages were useful only as retrospective evaluation or were omitted because they repeated the same 2022 shock without adding a new ruler-attributed choice. Where a page duplicated a claim already covered by a stronger official source, I kept the stronger source instead of padding the dossier.

**Remaining gaps**
- Direct evidence on Scholz personally selecting or empowering specific economic advisers is still mostly coalition- and cabinet-level rather than a clean appointment audit.
- Household-level distribution data are still thin. The relief measures clearly targeted workers, families, welfare recipients, commuters, and low-income households, but I do not yet have strong 2022 evidence on regional, gender, or median-household effects.
- More search would help on entrepreneurship and competition policy beyond crisis relief, especially on whether 2022 measures improved long-run investment conditions or mainly stabilized the shock.
